{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/258012-contracts-of-the-inferno","id":258012,"title":"Contracts of the Inferno","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-16T04:41:46-07:00","id":258012,"title":"Contracts of the Inferno","content":"These are a list of powers I wrote for a contract based on the theme of hell and classic powers of denizens therein. Let me know if you like, or have suggestions on improvement.<br /> <br /> <b>Sinner's Gaze (\u2022)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">With this clause, the changeling can determine what the target's Vice is.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Cost: 1 Glamour</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Dice Pool: Wits + Wyrd</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Action: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Catch: The changeling is standing on the target's shadow.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">--Results</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Dramatic Failure: The changeling gains misinformation about the target's Vice.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Failure: Nothing happens.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Success: The changeling learns what the target's primary Vice is, and gains insight on their most recent acts of sin relevant to said-Vice. Such actions are not always fully explained, however, and may be misinterpreted if not given enough time to fully investigate.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Exceptional Success: As with normal success, except the changeling can gain insight into even older acts of sin, perhaps ones that the subject does not even remember doing, whether because of the supernatural or psychological barriers. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Whispers of Temptation (\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The changeling gains the power to make a sinful action sound reasonable to those who listen. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Cost: 1 Glamour</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Dice Pool: Manipulation + Wyrd</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Action: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Catch: The changeling whispers in the target's ear.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">--Results</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Dramatic Failure: The target becomes appalled by the changeling's words, who gains a -5 to all social rolls with that target for the remainder of the scene.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Failure: Nothing happens.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Success: The changeling gains for one scene a +1 for every success they rolled to persuade the target to commit an action relevant to their vice. If the target's vice is Wrath, then the changeling would not gain any bonus for suggesting to the target to bonk the neighbor lady, but if it was Lust, then the bonus would apply.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Exceptional Success: As above, save it doesn't matter which vice the target has, all suggestions seem agreeable.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Devil's Puppetry (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">At this point in the contract, the changeling can now temporarily possess a given target. Doing so, however, leaves their body inert. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Cost: 2 Glamour</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Dice Pool: Manipulation + Wyrd vs. Composure + Wyrd</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Action: Contested; Prolonged</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Catch: The target must have signed something for the changeling.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">--Results</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Dramatic Failure: The changeling falls unconscious, and the target cannot be possessed by said changeling for another 13 days.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Failure: Nothing happens.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Success: If the target is within sensory range, the changeling's mind leaves their body and possesses them, granting full control over the target's body and its skills--but not its memories or supernatural abilities. While in control, the changeling cannot use any of his or her contracts, nor use any other changeling abilities. She may return to her real body whenever she wants, but doing so ends the clause. Once back in her body, the changeling will not remember any bits of information relevant to their victim's skills or merits. Example, she'll remember that she used to know Spanish, but won't be able to recite any facts about the language unless she already knew them before possession. The clause lasts a number of hours equal to the number of successes rolled. This clause cannot be used on a target being seen or heard through a medium, such as a camera or telephone.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Exceptional Success: Additional successes are their own reward.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Corruption Manifest (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">With this dread clause, a changeling can desecrate an area with dark glamour, making it harder to resist sinful activity while in its vicinity.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Cost: 3 Glamour</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Dice Pool: Presence + Wyrd</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Action: Instant; Prolonged</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Catch: The clause is used between Midnight and 3 o'clock in the morning.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">--Results</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Dramatic Failure: The changeling suffers nausea and cannot attempt to corrupt the area for another month.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Failure: Nothing happens.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Success: The area becomes corrupted by the power of sin, creating a -1 per success to all morality checks and attempts to resist acting on their vice. Meanwhile, all clauses under the Contract of the Inferno gain a +1 to dice pools when cast in the area, even if by another changeling. The effect lasts for an hour and a day.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Exceptional Success: The bonus to contract rolls becomes +2. Otherwise, additional successes are their own reward.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Hellfire (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The final and most dangerous of the contract's powers, the changeling summons raw hellfire to burn the wicked.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Cost: 3 Glamour + 1 Willpower point</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Dice Pool: Stamina + Wyrd</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Action: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Catch: The changeling is standing within a magic circle drawn in fresh blood.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">--Results</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Dramatic Failure: The changeling is burned by the flames, and suffers lethal damage equal to 10 minus their current morality score. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Failure: Nothing happens.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Success: The changeling conjures a smokeless black flame that erupts from out of thin air, causing lethal damage to anything in a radius of at most five yards. The fire is supernatural in nature, and does not damage mundane objects. However, with anything capable of thought, it manifests as lethal damage equal to 10 minus their current morality score. If the creature does not have a form of morality, such as with the Gentry or mindless constructs, then it suffers no damage. Fire proof substances do nothing to ward off the flames, but do drop it to doing bashing damage instead. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Exceptional Success: The fire does aggravated damage instead of lethal. If something obstructs it, the fire does lethal instead.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 09-16-2014, 07:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T12:42:11-07:00","id":259108,"title":"","content":"I'm assuming those who have bought these Contracts must give some sort of annual tithe to the entities that offer them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T13:08:55-07:00","id":259159,"title":"","content":"Up to the storyteller. But yeah, that's always a good plot hook in and of itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T20:21:13-07:00","id":265130,"title":"","content":"I like it, I can defiantly see there used by the Lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T13:26:35-07:00","id":265708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/258012-contracts-of-the-inferno?p=265130#post265130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it, I can defiantly see there used by the Lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Defiantly?&quot; :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T16:20:22-07:00","id":265783,"title":"","content":"Well, it would not be appropriate for all of the Lost but yeah I can see them using it,especially the ones whose Durance made them look practically like classical demons. Combine that with the fact that changelings are some the greatest bargainers in the world if darkness and you get yourself your own trickster Devil. <br /> <br /> <br /> Also what type of contract you think it would be, I would personally make it a Court contract that is part of a three-way court system based on Dante's Divine Comedy, <b> Court of Inferno </b> anguish, <b> Court of Purgatorio </b> remorse or guilt <b> Court of Paradiso </b> awe, but that's just me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T19:04:00-07:00","id":265873,"title":"","content":"I do like this concept and I will definitely be using it in my own nWoD game at some point. I think it makes sense. And, if we run a Changeling game and someone goes &quot;Hey, those things that Calamieu, Lord of Cats and Baron of the Winterflame Depths used on us that one time? Can I learn those?&quot; Yes, it is a Promethean game and yes, I love crossovers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T18:34:30-07:00","id":269699,"title":"","content":".... is it just me, or is this pretty much a straight lift of Daimonon from Masquerade? Not that I mind, but it seems really similar?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T21:32:27-07:00","id":269805,"title":"","content":"I used rules from the Equinox book, and got inspiration from the Inferno book. What does daimonon do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T05:49:12-08:00","id":304496,"title":"","content":"What if this was the Court Contract for a freehold stylized around Hell? Like the Ministries from Demon: The Fallen (Aurochs, Dragons, Dust, Eagles and Lions)? Granted, the names might need to be replaced to avoid limiting beast kiths...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T14:09:09-08:00","id":304975,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's just because I used that Autumn contract so much but I could see something along the lines of a contract to know the most sinful act the target ever commit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T15:11:52-08:00","id":326320,"title":"","content":"So ideal representations of this Contracts clauses in latest movie with Daniel Radcliffe about boy who become demon after his almost fiancee is found dead and all the town and family bleaming him for killing her. Just see this trailer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/3U7kcwiFsVM\" data-code=\"3U7kcwiFsVM\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/3U7kcwiFsVM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> I assure you, in the movie there are more stuff like this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> BTW: Is there possibility for mortal to become changeling without being taken by Gentry? Like in above exmaple, great personal trauma?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamst